frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268407} {:answer/id #uuid "bacea89d-b52f-5ee9-904d-b2cd1278e1b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268408} {:answer/id #uuid "28be3ccc-344e-53af-bee2-ca81a2990ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268409} {:answer/id #uuid "9a57b89b-3eda-5ba1-b7f6-d40046e52459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28be3ccc-344e-53af-bee2-ca81a2990ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268409} :answer-field/id #uuid "497ae8f6-9970-5421-8330-05484923f518" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268405}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38601207-2ed3-56b9-b15a-eeddc04bf3a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74579" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)}(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85555bce-debf-5165-ba6a-3c232deeeb0a" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5520354-a3cf-510f-b786-f59a3af18478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268413} {:answer/id #uuid "020ef4a0-3672-52b7-81af-1346c378c87d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268414} {:answer/id #uuid "106d5432-3f0a-58b1-9ba9-2b0430d65c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268415} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7ceb09-b044-52cf-acae-8247bb3ef412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268416} {:answer/id #uuid "868a0761-f4bf-59ba-891b-4e0d723b4dcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5520354-a3cf-510f-b786-f59a3af18478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268413} :answer-field/id #uuid "d09a68cf-ff4b-5870-86f3-e19c5298d345" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268412}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba944e9f-16ca-5b04-beb2-6ce54e9158c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-74580" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -2}{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -2}{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{2(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1)}(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
